    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, be points such that the area of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> sq. unit, then the sum of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is:",
